      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city’s name honors George Washington’s estate, linking the town to the nation’s first president.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Vernon%2C_Georgia",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Mount Vernon sits on high ground just east of the Oconee River, which historically served as the main transportation artery for the region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
